      <p>Chauffeur driving is deliberately unremarkable. Smooth braking, gentle lane changes and steady speeds make it possible to read, type or rest. It also reflects local experience. Knowing how traffic typically builds on I-395, I-66 and the George Washington Parkway, which downtown streets clog during the evening rush, and when a slightly longer route is the more reliable one comes only from driving these roads every day.</p>

